1
00:00:47,422 --> 00:00:49,674
Chiara and her group
will be traveling from Prague

2
00:00:49,758 --> 00:00:51,634
to meet with the Castellanis.

3
00:01:03,980 --> 00:01:06,066
He can't realize
that his phone is missing.

4
00:01:06,149 --> 00:01:07,609
So you better be on your way,

5
00:01:07,692 --> 00:01:09,652
or we'll lose our chance
to get La Fornarina.

6
00:01:09,736 --> 00:01:11,112
Just tell me which direction he's going.

7
00:01:21,998 --> 00:01:27,003
I hope your wish
is that everything goes smoothly tomorrow.

8
00:01:35,220 --> 00:01:37,305
<i>The background you're seeing behind me</i>

9
00:01:37,388 --> 00:01:39,098
<i>is called Piazza del Popolo.</i>

10
00:01:39,182 --> 00:01:43,937
This will also be Chiara's meeting place
with the leader of the Castellani family.

11
00:01:47,732 --> 00:01:48,942
<i>Francesco Castellani.</i>

12
00:01:49,025 --> 00:01:51,069
Why does La Fornarina need

13
00:01:51,152 --> 00:01:53,196
to meet with the Castellani family?

14
00:01:53,279 --> 00:01:54,948
<i>If she gets their support,</i>

15
00:01:55,031 --> 00:01:58,660
<i>then Chiara's hold on power over all</i>
<i>the mafias in Europe will strengthen.</i>

16
00:02:12,132 --> 00:02:15,802
So we can ensure
that we are getting good intelligence.

17
00:02:24,269 --> 00:02:25,395
We're on the same side.

18
00:02:25,478 --> 00:02:29,357
We both want justice for his death.

19
00:02:29,440 --> 00:02:31,317
I'm not your enemy here.

20
00:02:33,319 --> 00:02:36,489
And believe it or not, I trust you.

21
00:02:37,073 --> 00:02:39,492
But with the recent case of Sianong
turning out to be a mole,

22
00:02:40,243 --> 00:02:41,703
an enemy plant,

23
00:02:41,786 --> 00:02:44,497
I need to take any necessary precaution,

24
00:02:44,998 --> 00:02:46,499
just to keep my asset safe.

25
00:03:03,600 --> 00:03:06,436
Even the next generation of their family.

26
00:03:06,519 --> 00:03:07,937
Because honestly,

27
00:03:08,897 --> 00:03:10,899
I'm tired of dealing with them.

28
00:03:11,441 --> 00:03:13,943
I'm just giving them a chance
because of you.

29
00:03:18,489 --> 00:03:19,908
They are stubborn,

30
00:03:19,991 --> 00:03:22,577
but they're not unreasonable.

31
00:03:26,122 --> 00:03:27,582
I told you,

32
00:03:27,665 --> 00:03:32,003
it's better to talk things out
than to try killing each other.

33
00:04:44,117 --> 00:04:45,201
Come in.

34
00:04:45,702 --> 00:04:47,954
Good evening, sir. You have a visitor.

35
00:04:52,542 --> 00:04:53,918
Good evening, General.

36
00:04:54,002 --> 00:04:55,878
- Good evening, General.
- Good evening.

37
00:04:56,671 --> 00:04:57,839
You?

38
00:04:59,132 --> 00:05:01,759
No, sir. It's Sister Tess, sir.

39
00:05:03,344 --> 00:05:04,554
Tess.

40
00:05:14,814 --> 00:05:15,773
Are you avoiding me?

41
00:05:16,858 --> 00:05:17,984
Brother Mikoy!

42
00:05:22,155 --> 00:05:23,573
No, I didn't know it was you.

43
00:05:23,656 --> 00:05:25,533
I thought someone was chasing me.

44
00:05:28,161 --> 00:05:30,246
You? How are you?

45
00:05:30,747 --> 00:05:31,914
How's Mom Tess?

46
00:05:32,623 --> 00:05:34,083
You know her.

47
00:05:34,167 --> 00:05:36,044
She's the strongest of us all.

48
00:05:36,127 --> 00:05:39,505
Even though she's hurting inside,
she'd never show it to me.

49
00:05:45,595 --> 00:05:46,721
Sorry, Brother Mikoy.

50
00:05:48,473 --> 00:05:50,600
I didn't mean for this to happen.

51
00:06:00,151 --> 00:06:02,070
I didn't tell anyone
that you're my informant.

52
00:06:06,115 --> 00:06:07,784
But I need your help.

53
00:06:11,788 --> 00:06:14,499
So Dad's death won't be for nothing.

54
00:06:19,003 --> 00:06:20,046
Yes, Bro.

55
00:06:35,353 --> 00:06:37,021
I'm sorry, okay?

56
00:06:39,232 --> 00:06:43,861
I don't know if this is urgent
based on your agency's protocol.

57
00:06:45,613 --> 00:06:47,615
But as a mother,

58
00:06:48,407 --> 00:06:50,743
when it comes to my son,
everything is urgent.

59
00:06:51,244 --> 00:06:52,787
Everything is important.

60
00:06:54,163 --> 00:06:56,207
I understand, Tess.

61
00:06:58,459 --> 00:07:02,380
A parent's concern can come at any hour.

62
00:07:05,383 --> 00:07:07,051
Is this about Mikoy?

63
00:07:09,762 --> 00:07:12,390
Norberto, I just can't shake this feeling.

64
00:07:13,349 --> 00:07:16,894
And I don't have anyone else to talk to
who would understand me.

65
00:07:18,062 --> 00:07:19,814
Don't worry.

66
00:07:20,565 --> 00:07:23,234
Agent Alex is with Mikoy.

67
00:07:23,317 --> 00:07:26,946
The best agent in this agency.

68
00:07:29,449 --> 00:07:32,243
You know, I do trust Agent Alex.

69
00:07:32,326 --> 00:07:35,288
And I know you're all doing
everything you can

70
00:07:35,371 --> 00:07:37,540
to keep them both safe.

71
00:07:37,623 --> 00:07:40,418
But it's Mikoy I'm worried about.

72
00:07:41,419 --> 00:07:43,296
It's like he's changed.

73
00:07:44,464 --> 00:07:47,258
And I know that you know what I mean.

74
00:07:52,221 --> 00:07:57,602
I know Mikoy is old enough
to make his own decisions about his life.

75
00:07:59,520 --> 00:08:01,355
But I still can't shake this feeling.

76
00:08:03,733 --> 00:08:05,234
He even told me

77
00:08:05,318 --> 00:08:07,820
that this would really be
his last mission.

78
00:08:10,239 --> 00:08:12,575
But no matter what he says,

79
00:08:12,658 --> 00:08:14,744
I don't believe him.

80
00:08:17,330 --> 00:08:24,086
Because I know that he's doing this
out of sadness and anger.

81
00:08:25,796 --> 00:08:27,423
But Norberto,

82
00:08:28,299 --> 00:08:30,092
that's not who my son is.

83
00:08:31,928 --> 00:08:33,471
You know Mikoy.

84
00:08:34,347 --> 00:08:35,973
Every decision he makes

85
00:08:38,351 --> 00:08:40,061
is because of love.

86
00:08:43,397 --> 00:08:45,691
I'm really worried about Mikoy.

87
00:08:46,817 --> 00:08:48,194
And you're right.

88
00:08:49,612 --> 00:08:52,114
A lot has changed in Mikoy's life.

89
00:08:53,074 --> 00:08:55,409
What happened to him was no small thing.

90
00:08:56,953 --> 00:08:59,622
It's like fate itself
was playing a cruel joke on him.

91
00:09:02,124 --> 00:09:05,253
But in all my years with this agency,

92
00:09:06,045 --> 00:09:10,841
I've seen how pain, sadness,

93
00:09:11,425 --> 00:09:13,386
and anger can change a person.

94
00:09:16,764 --> 00:09:19,016
But I also believe

95
00:09:19,559 --> 00:09:22,478
that Mikoy needs to go through this.

96
00:09:23,396 --> 00:09:27,817
He needs to face the truth.

97
00:09:29,402 --> 00:09:30,319
Face it?

98
00:09:31,696 --> 00:09:33,823
Even if it puts his life at risk?

99
00:09:33,906 --> 00:09:34,991
Even if it gets him killed?

100
00:09:37,076 --> 00:09:39,996
I wouldn't let that happen, Norberto.

101
00:09:42,665 --> 00:09:45,334
I know that here in this agency,

102
00:09:45,960 --> 00:09:49,589
you're like a parent
to all the agents here.

103
00:09:51,757 --> 00:09:55,761
And Mikoy has so much respect for you.

104
00:09:56,887 --> 00:10:01,100
Maybe there's still time
to call off the mission?

105
00:10:03,102 --> 00:10:06,022
Maybe Mikoy could just come home to us.

106
00:10:07,898 --> 00:10:10,401
We're just ordinary people, after all.

107
00:10:12,820 --> 00:10:16,282
And this isn't the kind of dangerous life
I want for my son.

108
00:10:20,328 --> 00:10:23,664
We want Mikoy to be safe too.

109
00:10:25,625 --> 00:10:30,087
We're doing everything we can
to make sure no innocent people get hurt.

110
00:10:31,839 --> 00:10:32,715
Tess,

111
00:10:34,050 --> 00:10:35,676
we're on your side.

112
00:10:38,304 --> 00:10:39,847
You can count on me.

113
00:11:04,413 --> 00:11:06,290
Has Francesco made a move?

114
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:09,251
Not yet.

115
00:11:15,091 --> 00:11:16,133
Cheers.

116
00:11:22,306 --> 00:11:24,016
What is this? Why does it taste like this?

117
00:11:24,892 --> 00:11:26,602
Keep drinking. You'll get used to it.

118
00:11:34,360 --> 00:11:36,946
You know, don't worry
about Francesco anymore.

119
00:11:38,239 --> 00:11:39,949
He has nowhere else to go.

120
00:11:40,741 --> 00:11:43,077
I've hacked the CCTV around the hotel,

121
00:11:43,160 --> 00:11:46,330
so we'll have eyes
on every movement in and out.

122
00:11:50,126 --> 00:11:51,836
I didn't know

123
00:11:53,212 --> 00:11:54,630
you were this techy.

124
00:11:57,550 --> 00:11:59,802
I guess it's one of the things
Agent Sianong taught me

125
00:11:59,885 --> 00:12:01,262
and passed on to me.

126
00:12:04,557 --> 00:12:05,683
But…

127
00:12:07,351 --> 00:12:09,186
You know what's been bothering me?

128
00:12:12,648 --> 00:12:15,151
What was actually real
about everything he showed us?

129
00:12:16,694 --> 00:12:18,821
Was he just pretending all this time?

130
00:12:25,494 --> 00:12:27,371
You might be forgetting

131
00:12:27,913 --> 00:12:30,166
that I pretended
to be someone else to Chiara too.

132
00:12:35,421 --> 00:12:38,090
Just because we lied about one thing

133
00:12:38,757 --> 00:12:41,719
doesn't mean everything we showed everyone
about ourselves was a lie.

134
00:12:44,972 --> 00:12:46,223
For example,

135
00:12:51,020 --> 00:12:55,357
Even though those seven habits
didn't believe in him.

136
00:12:56,317 --> 00:12:57,234
Right?

137
00:13:00,905 --> 00:13:02,239
You're right.

138
00:13:03,324 --> 00:13:04,909
Of all people,

139
00:13:05,409 --> 00:13:08,204
you're the one who knows
Agent Sianong more.

140
00:13:09,663 --> 00:13:11,165
But I would like to say

141
00:13:12,291 --> 00:13:14,919
that I understand him more.

142
00:13:18,923 --> 00:13:19,757
Why?

143
00:13:22,343 --> 00:13:24,386
Are you also a <i>Lord of the Rings</i> fan?

144
00:13:26,597 --> 00:13:27,932
That's not it.

145
00:13:31,560 --> 00:13:32,937
I thought it was.

146
00:13:34,271 --> 00:13:35,147
Then what?

147
00:13:37,900 --> 00:13:40,027
Because in other areas of life,

148
00:13:41,362 --> 00:13:43,030
we're exactly the same.

149
00:13:46,492 --> 00:13:47,952
We both fell in love.

150
00:13:54,583 --> 00:13:57,086
We both love someone
who is in love with someone else.

151
00:14:43,173 --> 00:14:45,467
No, no, you don't have to apologize.

152
00:14:47,386 --> 00:14:48,679
By the way,

153
00:14:48,762 --> 00:14:50,514
I forgot to buy something
from the convenience store.

154
00:14:51,098 --> 00:14:52,266
You monitor things for now.

155
00:14:52,349 --> 00:14:55,227
And when you get tired, just let me know.

156
00:14:55,311 --> 00:14:56,645
I'll take over.

157
00:15:18,959 --> 00:15:20,252
Sir, excuse me.

158
00:15:21,420 --> 00:15:23,714
I think your companion already left.

159
00:15:24,715 --> 00:15:26,175
Our companion, Sister Tess?

160
00:15:26,258 --> 00:15:28,844
Yes, sir. She just went out.

161
00:15:28,928 --> 00:15:30,638
Hey.

162
00:15:30,721 --> 00:15:32,306
- They said it was Sister Tess.
- Sister Tess?

163
00:15:32,389 --> 00:15:33,974
Wait, hold on, my juice.

164
00:15:34,475 --> 00:15:35,809
Say thanks for the juice.

165
00:15:45,194 --> 00:15:48,113
Keep your voice down.
Someone might hear you.

166
00:15:48,739 --> 00:15:49,823
Well, it's your fault!

167
00:15:49,907 --> 00:15:52,618
That bomb you dropped was insane.

168
00:15:53,202 --> 00:15:54,119
What happened?

169
00:15:55,287 --> 00:15:57,581
Nothing. Nothing happened.

170
00:15:58,248 --> 00:15:59,124
Of course.

171
00:16:03,253 --> 00:16:04,797
What did you expect?

172
00:16:05,464 --> 00:16:09,009
That's why I called you, so I could vent.

173
00:16:10,177 --> 00:16:11,428
I don't even know.

174
00:16:11,512 --> 00:16:14,431
I'm such an idiot. I wasn't thinking.
I just acted on impulse.

175
00:16:14,932 --> 00:16:16,809
<i>I knew it.</i>

176
00:16:16,892 --> 00:16:19,103
This mission wasn't a good idea.

177
00:16:19,186 --> 00:16:21,522
Your mission there in Italy.

178
00:16:35,953 --> 00:16:39,456
<i>But the agency has no choice</i>
<i>because Chiara knows too much.</i>

179
00:16:50,968 --> 00:16:52,970
That's also my struggle, Agent Dara.

180
00:16:53,804 --> 00:16:56,473
And I know this is an unnecessary evil.

181
00:16:58,308 --> 00:17:00,060
But as long as Chiara is alive,

182
00:17:00,686 --> 00:17:02,146
we will not be safe.

183
00:17:07,985 --> 00:17:11,989
I know he won't stop until he gets justice
for his father's death.

184
00:17:17,745 --> 00:17:19,663
Sometimes I feel like

185
00:17:19,747 --> 00:17:24,710
this is a government-sanctioned
revenge plot for Mikoy.

186
00:17:25,335 --> 00:17:27,421
<i>And for General Norberto,</i>

187
00:17:27,504 --> 00:17:29,673
<i>who was a friend of Sir Mario.</i>

188
00:17:29,757 --> 00:17:35,387
<i>And I find the justification</i>
<i>for assassinating Chiara very thin.</i>

189
00:18:02,247 --> 00:18:05,250
<i>Sir, I'm very disappointed</i>
<i>that you left me behind here.</i>

190
00:18:06,085 --> 00:18:08,295
<i>I thought it was supposed to be</i>
<i>until the end of time.</i>

191
00:18:22,935 --> 00:18:24,520
Please take my daughter.

192
00:18:44,248 --> 00:18:47,292
What happened to the GAGO?

193
00:19:12,818 --> 00:19:13,735
Mikoy.

194
00:19:22,953 --> 00:19:24,413
About what happened yesterday.

195
00:19:28,083 --> 00:19:29,751
Are we really not going to talk about it?

196
00:19:31,795 --> 00:19:32,880
Just forget about it.

197
00:19:35,174 --> 00:19:36,842
I can't just forget about it, Mikoy.

198
00:19:43,807 --> 00:19:44,641
Why?

199
00:19:54,026 --> 00:19:55,402
What I feel for you

200
00:19:55,986 --> 00:19:57,613
makes it complicated.

201
00:19:58,238 --> 00:19:59,072
Why?

202
00:20:00,407 --> 00:20:02,201
Do you think I still love her?

203
00:20:03,285 --> 00:20:05,120
That I still have feelings for her?

204
00:20:07,080 --> 00:20:09,291
Why? You don't anymore?

205
00:20:17,591 --> 00:20:18,800
This isn't Prague.

206
00:20:25,682 --> 00:20:27,517
Even though I am a <i>tifosi</i>.

207
00:20:33,774 --> 00:20:37,569
The Castellani family won't dare
do anything stupid here.

208
00:21:04,471 --> 00:21:08,100
Does it matter
if I still have feelings for her?

209
00:21:09,434 --> 00:21:11,436
Alex, she killed my father.

210
00:21:16,149 --> 00:21:19,736
She turned her back on me
and left me like a fucking idiot.

211
00:21:23,865 --> 00:21:26,410
Will that make
my feelings for her disappear?

212
00:21:29,788 --> 00:21:31,373
You know, honestly, I don't know.

213
00:21:31,873 --> 00:21:33,458
But I don't care.

214
00:21:33,959 --> 00:21:35,919
Because all my heart wants right now

215
00:21:36,795 --> 00:21:39,214
is to get justice
for what she did to my father.

216
00:21:41,300 --> 00:21:43,302
So tell me, Agent Alex,

217
00:21:44,261 --> 00:21:48,724
that you can do what needs to be done
when the time comes.

218
00:22:04,698 --> 00:22:06,283
What is that? A new K-pop group?

219
00:22:06,366 --> 00:22:08,410
I wish it were K-pop.

220
00:22:47,240 --> 00:22:48,283
I will.

221
00:23:14,810 --> 00:23:16,228
La Fornarina.

222
00:23:17,813 --> 00:23:20,023
- They only have one request.
- What is that?

223
00:23:20,107 --> 00:23:24,903
Just me, Chiara, and a few bodyguards.

224
00:23:28,323 --> 00:23:29,157
What's happening?

225
00:23:29,241 --> 00:23:31,118
The Castellanis made last-minute changes.

226
00:23:31,201 --> 00:23:32,869
They changed the meeting place for Chiara.

227
00:23:38,583 --> 00:23:39,709
Leave them be for now.

228
00:23:46,591 --> 00:23:48,176
You stay here on the ground, okay?

229
00:23:48,260 --> 00:23:49,553
Okay, take care.

230
00:23:51,471 --> 00:23:53,390
<i>We can't act recklessly.</i>

231
00:23:53,473 --> 00:23:55,058
<i>We haven't scouted the area yet.</i>
